{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/786123-seeming-for-freed-changelings","id":786123,"title":"Seeming for 'Freed' Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-14T12:20:50-08:00","id":786123,"title":"Seeming for 'Freed' Changelings","content":"After reading through the development logs for the seemings, I was wondering what would happen to Changelings that where 'allowed' to leave for whatever reason by their keeper? Do they just not get a seeming and are left only with their kith? If so I hope that the new seeming coming in Dark Era's is built for changelings that where freed since I'm not sure I want to miss out on the blessing and curse mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","name":"Faster-Than-FedEx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T12:58:30-08:00","id":786152,"title":"","content":"If you're freed, you haven't mutated yourself with a promise to the world you were residing in to be larger than it, in some way. So, freed changelings are Seemingless, and only have their kith.<br /> <br /> No Seeming will ever be awarded to a changeling who doesn't do something to free themselves. Even the idea of the Loyalist involves a changeling freeing themselves by binding themselves to powers larger than themselves. A Seeming is for those who <i>act,</i> who decides to do something to free themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-14-2015, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T13:30:33-08:00","id":786184,"title":"","content":"Ah, well I'm not a fan of that so I guess I'll be homeruling out the 2e version of seemings, oh well. Thank you for the prompt answer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","name":"Faster-Than-FedEx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T14:07:45-08:00","id":786220,"title":"","content":"No problem. Shame you dislike it-I feel like it empowers the Seemings and creates some interesting dynamics between Seeming characters and non-seeming characters-but hey, what works for you man. Go out and have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T14:23:34-08:00","id":786242,"title":"","content":"You can stretch the definition of Agency a bit to find the closest Seeming. It's practically unheard of for True Fae to simply squander their investment into a captured mortal while they are still useful. Even if you do something so outrageous and insane that even your Keeper starts doubting if it's a good idea to have you around, that could turn you into a Beast. Sure, your Keeper opened the gate and flat out told you to never come back, but they only did so because of something YOU did.<br /> <br /> That's how I see it, at least.<br /> <br /> As for the possibility of developing a Seeming after leaving Arcadia? I don't think the rules will support that. Between the 6 standard Seemings and the ones coming up in the Dark Eras, you can certainly find a good enough fit if you put some more thought into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-14-2015, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T14:29:54-08:00","id":786251,"title":"","content":"We might have something for post-Durance Seemings in a later book. We'll see once the core is out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T19:47:52-08:00","id":786457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faster-Than-FedEx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/786123-seeming-for-freed-changelings#post786123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was wondering what would happen to Changelings that where 'allowed' to leave <b>for whatever reason</b> by their keeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;whatever reason&quot; is rather important with this, and could be the difference between no seeming and a seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T22:24:10-08:00","id":786520,"title":"","content":"If the True Fae just got tired of you and dumped you into the Hedge, that would not give you a Seeming. If you manged to trick, impress, or otherwise /earn/ release that's a different story- literally.<br /> <br /> You catch your Keeper in a turn of phrase to sign a Pledge on their True Name- they must agree to do whatever you wish or break the Pledge, which would mean total anihilation- a total and complete death. Darkling for the underhanded and Gentry - like deception. Maybe you had to climb over your fellow slaves to get to such a position of trust to begin with. Maybe such disregard for Pledges is a sufficient bucking of tradition to warrant a Beast.<br /> <br /> You actually complete your impossible task- maybe by sheer skill, maybe by the goodwill of others you sacrificed for along the way. Maybe you just lost yourself in the task and drifted off. Wizened, Fairest, Elemental.<br /> <br /> I'm having a little trouble coming up with one for Ogres, the Grimm Changelings, or those Fate - based ones. Were they ever confirmed or were they just a rumour? Heck, maybe a Changeling who was &quot;let go&quot; agreed to do something for the Gentry. A Loyalist by trade if not in their heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T22:57:58-08:00","id":786528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/786123-seeming-for-freed-changelings?p=786520#post786520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">those Fate - based ones. Were they ever confirmed or were they just a rumour? Heck, maybe a Changeling who was &quot;let go&quot; agreed to do something for the Gentry. A Loyalist by trade if not in their heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc it was the opposite, random rather than fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T23:38:44-08:00","id":786540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/786123-seeming-for-freed-changelings?p=786520#post786520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the True Fae just got tired of you and dumped you into the Hedge, that would not give you a Seeming. If you manged to trick, impress, or otherwise /earn/ release that's a different story- literally. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well my plan was to play as a bloodbrute and play into the built in connection to arena's and have her be a gladiator in her keepers Coliseum and over time win her freedom. I'm sure that in a way could be connected to ogre's because of the violence/earning her freedom through the pain/deaths of others. The ultimate reason behind the Coliseum letting her go was in hopes she'd either come back stronger to fight again or would reach high wyrd/low clarity and become a new True Fae.<br /> <br /> Honestly the main problem for me in most Seemings is the wording and how I interpret them, they all fell more like strict guidelines than suggestions examples so I'm hoping that the finished version will have wording that gives that feeling off more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","user":"Faster-Than-FedEx","date":".  Spelling and wrong terminology. It's late. 12-15-2015, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","name":"Faster-Than-FedEx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T01:07:46-08:00","id":786570,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Winning your freedom would be enough to get a seeming (as long as you think your winning your freedom).</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Honestly the main problem for me in most Seemings is the wording and how I interpret them, they all fell more like strict guidelines than suggestions examples so I'm hoping that the finished version will have wording that gives that feeling off more.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">This sort of thing has been said many times, and each time I am sincerely curious as to how that interpretation is gained. Here's a few examples for this situation:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Beast, if he breaks the rules of the Coliseum.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Darkling, since he killed other changelings just to escape.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Elemental, you wanted to be the best warrior, you Needed to be the best or you would never escape... but over time you eventually realized you had no chance, you could never be the best. But from that acceptance something crawled into your now hollow soul, something primal.<br /> Fairest, after defeating his final opponent, he is ordered to kill the champion to earn his freedom, but he rejects the idea, not wanting to kill another simply wanting to escape. That sacrifice amazed the audience and the fellow fighters so much that the Gentry could not deny the changeling's escape.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Ogre, he could have never killed his </span>opponents<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> over and over, simply incapacitated them, until his last battle where the rules say he must kill the champion to earn his freedom.</span><br /> Wizened, as he goes from battle to battle, his wounds grow, but he did not want to risk weakening between bouts, so he healed his wounds with armour pieces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T12:05:34-08:00","id":786837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're freed, you haven't mutated yourself with a promise to the world you were residing in to be larger than it, in some way. So, freed changelings are Seemingless, and only have their kith.<br /> <br /> No Seeming will ever be awarded to a changeling who doesn't do something to free themselves. Even the idea of the Loyalist involves a changeling freeing themselves by binding themselves to powers larger than themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like this. I can envision the ways loyalists could earn seemings but remain under the control of their keepers, it is particularly easy to see in the case of Darklings (Betrayal to earn your limited freedom as their agent in the material world, kind of the picture of a loyalist privateer), Ogres(Same as darkling but with violence), Wizened (same as darkling but with skill), Beasts ( picturing feral hunting hounds of the fae that just give in and become hunting beasts mentally to be let off the chain to hunt down its prey), and particularly tragic Fairest (aw, he's doing it for the greater good for those still held hostage, doesn't that make you feel better that you are being carted back to Arcadia? no? huh, me either.), but elemental is a little abstract for me, but I get dim pictures of an example of some elemental being that wisps people away to the greater will of their True Fae patron.<br /> <br /> All those specific examples of how having a seem doesn't mean you're not a loyalist, it would still mean that if you don't have a seeming you are much more likely to be either a metaphorical damsel in distress that was saved without agency, or a 'sleeper' agent of True Fae serving without agency, and the smart money isn't on the former. I do see most Loyalists who are also privateers qualifying for a seeming, by nature of their service that grants them access to the mortal world. The vast majority, loyalist or not, would have seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-15-2015, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T14:00:04-08:00","id":787618,"title":"","content":"I think it seems cool that people who were saved (say by a raid of changelings who liberate them) don't earn any seemings.<br /> It could almost act like a social stigma too.<br /> &quot;No we don't talk to Bob. Fucking seamingless prick. My two closest friends died to save his ass.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}